## 5. Resource Estimate
The projected delivery model requires a cross-functional team composed of one QA lead, one SDET/automation engineer, one performance engineer shared part-time, one AppSec resource shared for scan review, one release engineer for pipeline and environment orchestration, and support from development for log instrumentation and defect remediation. Given the feature’s integration complexity, the resource estimate assumes focused collaboration rather than isolated QA execution. The QA lead owns planning, traceability, risk review, and go/no-go evidence. The SDET owns Playwright and PyTest implementation. The performance engineer owns JMeter thresholds and timing interpretation. Release engineering owns tcconfig integration, pipeline controls, and artifact publication.

Estimated timeline: 2 business days for test design finalization and traceability mapping; 4 business days for automation enhancement and fixture preparation; 2 business days for integrated QA execution and defect triage; 2 business days for Pre-Prod performance/security execution and retest; 1 business day for final evidence review and Gate 3 approval. Total elapsed estimate is approximately 11 business days, assuming stable environments and prompt engineering response. If major integration defects are discovered in scanner ordering, cache invalidation, or gateway routing, add 3 to 5 business days for remediation and repeat qualification.

