## 11. Human-Readable Executive Report
The test strategy for AD-488 has been compiled to address the complete avatar upload and crop release risk profile, not merely the happy-path upload behavior. The document intentionally validates the interaction between authentication gating, gateway enforcement, binary validation, synchronous malware scanning, storage authorization, CDN cache invalidation, and real-time UI synchronization. This depth is necessary because a seemingly small avatar feature crosses multiple trust boundaries and can fail in ways that are not visible to a casual smoke test. The strategy therefore emphasizes proof of execution order, side-effect suppression, and deterministic latency measurement.

Implementation should proceed in the following order. First, validate environment readiness and observability coverage so that critical conditions such as scan-before-store ordering and gateway-only rejection can be measured with confidence. Second, complete automation uplift in Playwright and PyTest with explicit crop coverage, exact-size fixtures, unauthorized side-effect suppression checks, and multi-session synchronization validation. Third, execute integrated QA cycles and triage defects rapidly, prioritizing any issues affecting authentication enforcement, malware ordering, stale-cache propagation, or 2.0 second SLA compliance. Fourth, run Pre-Prod performance and security gates using JMeter, OWASP ZAP, and tcconfig, and refuse promotion if deterministic timing or security thresholds are not met.

During Human-in-the-Loop Gate 3, pipeline state must remain Paused until manual validation confirms that residual risk is acceptable, evidence is complete, and any waivers are formally approved. Once approved, the strategy supports progression into final release readiness review and reporting-module handoff. The recommended next actions are: finalize test fixtures, verify branch protections and PR checks, execute integrated suites in QA, complete Pre-Prod SLA and security validation, and convene the final go/no-go meeting with documented evidence and risk disposition for AD-488.